1
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:53,345
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

2
00:00:53,471 --> 00:00:54,305
ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:54,472 --> 00:00:55,306
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

4
00:00:55,431 --> 00:00:56,265
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

5
00:01:15,201 --> 00:01:17,328
Put the Moon Donuts

6
00:01:17,453 --> 00:01:18,954
-behind the Chili Crunch.
-Hold on.

7
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:20,247
Swap their places.

8
00:01:20,831 --> 00:01:22,500
No, Chili Crunch should be in front.

9
00:01:23,292 --> 00:01:24,794
Are you disrespecting Moon Donuts?

10
00:01:24,919 --> 00:01:26,712
Chili Crunch generates far more revenue.

11
00:01:26,837 --> 00:01:27,671
It's too far back.

12
00:01:27,797 --> 00:01:29,590
-Move it forward.
-Okay.

13
00:01:29,715 --> 00:01:30,883
Look…

14
00:01:31,008 --> 00:01:32,134
Yes, that's perfect.

15
00:01:32,259 --> 00:01:34,178
That's way too far in front.

16
00:01:34,303 --> 00:01:36,013
Finally, the Hot Chocolate Chips.

17
00:01:36,138 --> 00:01:37,515
Where should this go?

18
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:40,184
It used to be our company's
best-selling product.

19
00:01:40,309 --> 00:01:42,353
Should we put it right in the center?

20
00:01:42,478 --> 00:01:45,397
If Spicy SweeTato Chips were released,
they could've been here together.

21
00:01:45,523 --> 00:01:47,858
Wait, could you come
hold this for a second?

22
00:01:47,983 --> 00:01:48,818
Come on.

23
00:01:48,943 --> 00:01:50,152
Should I hold the bottom?

24
00:01:50,277 --> 00:01:51,612
No, it's fine. Move that…

25
00:01:51,737 --> 00:01:53,781
BROTHER CLEANING

26
00:01:55,658 --> 00:01:58,160
-Is Namgung ignoring your calls, too?
-Forget it.

27
00:01:58,285 --> 00:02:00,120
It's for the best, for Namgung's sake.

28
00:02:00,246 --> 00:02:01,831
Who could even handle Mi-do?

29
00:02:02,665 --> 00:02:03,916
Look who's talking.

30
00:02:04,041 --> 00:02:05,835
Jeez, you scared me!

31
00:02:06,585 --> 00:02:10,422
You were whining about being broke
when you wanted to get married.

32
00:02:10,548 --> 00:02:13,342
So I helped you get married,
then you got divorced.

33
00:02:13,467 --> 00:02:16,011
Wow, how pathetic.

34
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:17,721
Why are you bringing that up?

35
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:21,475
It's not like you bought me a house.

36
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:23,602
It was only like five million won.

37
00:02:24,728 --> 00:02:25,938
"Only five million won"?

38
00:02:26,063 --> 00:02:26,897
Hey!

39
00:02:28,065 --> 00:02:30,484
Someone with 100 million
lending five million

40
00:02:30,609 --> 00:02:33,153
and someone with ten million
lending five million…

41
00:02:33,279 --> 00:02:34,196
No, wait.

42
00:02:34,321 --> 00:02:35,781
Someone with 5.12 million won

43
00:02:35,906 --> 00:02:37,867
lending five million is not the same.

44
00:02:37,992 --> 00:02:41,745
The value is completely different!

45
00:02:41,871 --> 00:02:45,249
I gave you my entire life savings
at the time, okay?

46
00:02:47,334 --> 00:02:50,212
That five million
wasn't just five million.

47
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:53,090
It was worth
more than 500 million won.

48
00:02:53,215 --> 00:02:56,927
So you have no right
to use the word "only"!

49
00:02:57,052 --> 00:02:58,095
Got it?

50
00:02:58,220 --> 00:03:00,639
Did I not pay you back? I paid you back.

51
00:03:00,764 --> 00:03:04,018
Did you even hear a word I just said?

52
00:03:04,685 --> 00:03:07,521
That five million was worth
over 500 million,

53
00:03:07,646 --> 00:03:10,482
so you should've paid back
500 million, you idiot!

54
00:03:10,608 --> 00:03:11,442
What a crook.

55
00:03:11,567 --> 00:03:13,068
A crook? You're an idiot,
so you're a crook--

56
00:03:13,193 --> 00:03:15,112
-Then I--
-Stop it, both of you!

57
00:03:21,827 --> 00:03:23,203
I'm going to throw up.

58
00:04:07,164 --> 00:04:11,794
To my deeply beloved Namgung-Tush.

59
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:20,636
Must be nice.

60
00:04:20,761 --> 00:04:23,138
The girl you had a crush on forever

61
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:24,765
finally became yours.

62
00:04:26,809 --> 00:04:29,853
Treat me right.
You still have a long way to go.

63
00:04:29,979 --> 00:04:31,313
Try harder.

64
00:04:31,438 --> 00:04:32,439
What the hell?

65
00:04:35,693 --> 00:04:37,653
YEONG-DO

66
00:04:38,988 --> 00:04:41,532
-What's up?
-We're in big trouble. What do we do?

67
00:04:41,657 --> 00:04:43,075
Mi-do's missing.

68
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:44,076
What?

69
00:04:44,785 --> 00:04:46,036
I'm losing my mind.

70
00:04:46,745 --> 00:04:48,205
Where the hell did she go?

71
00:04:48,330 --> 00:04:50,833
You need to get over here. I'm at…

72
00:04:53,877 --> 00:04:55,713
Why would I go there?

73
00:04:55,838 --> 00:04:57,715
I told you I broke up with her.

74
00:04:59,133 --> 00:05:01,301
Check the playground.
Look in the tube slide.

75
00:05:01,427 --> 00:05:03,679
You're going to make up anyway.

76
00:05:03,804 --> 00:05:05,431
Aren't you worried about Lee Mi-do?

77
00:05:05,973 --> 00:05:08,642
-If something happens--
-What does that have to do with me?

78
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:10,269
She and I are strangers now.

79
00:05:10,394 --> 00:05:12,354
I'm just going to do whatever I want.

80
00:05:13,272 --> 00:05:15,649
I'll join a matchmaking agency
and go on blind dates.

81
00:05:15,774 --> 00:05:16,608
And also,

82
00:05:16,734 --> 00:05:18,986
I'll go on  I Am Solo Too,
Single's Paradise,  all of them!

83
00:05:32,624 --> 00:05:34,418
TO MY DEEPLY BELOVED NAMGUNG-TUSH

84
00:05:57,357 --> 00:06:00,360
Do you have volume eight of  Slam Dunk?

85
00:06:36,855 --> 00:06:42,736
2. CAN WE EVER BE STRANGERS?

86
00:06:44,696 --> 00:06:46,824
NON-DISCLOSURE
AND RELATIONSHIP TERMINATION AGREEMENT

87
00:06:46,949 --> 00:06:47,825
This agreement states

88
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:51,495
you won't reveal
your relationship with the CEO.

89
00:07:01,797 --> 00:07:04,258
SIGNATURE

90
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:12,224
Oh, right.

91
00:07:13,142 --> 00:07:16,103
I'll be taking care of the matter
regarding Director Lee.

92
00:07:16,228 --> 00:07:17,354
You heard, right?

93
00:07:25,362 --> 00:07:27,030
This is Attorney Han Tae-seung.

94
00:07:27,156 --> 00:07:29,408
I heard through Producer Oh Yeon-ju
that you declined.

95
00:07:29,533 --> 00:07:32,161
Let's meet one more time
and try to work things out.

96
00:07:33,036 --> 00:07:34,788
I look forward to your response.

97
00:07:35,622 --> 00:07:39,126
If we go to trial, you'll lose
money, time, and emotional energy,

98
00:07:39,251 --> 00:07:41,003
not to mention your reputation.

99
00:07:41,545 --> 00:07:43,380
Why would you choose the hard way?

100
00:07:43,922 --> 00:07:45,424
I'll wait for your call.

101
00:07:48,969 --> 00:07:50,679
Ms. Lee, I handled your mediation request

102
00:07:50,804 --> 00:07:53,265
that you submitted
to the Film Industry Grievance Portal.

103
00:07:53,390 --> 00:07:55,517
It'd hurt both sides if this went public.

104
00:07:56,143 --> 00:07:57,394
I'll wait for your call.

105
00:07:57,519 --> 00:07:59,062
This bastard!

106
00:08:09,156 --> 00:08:10,365
25TH

107
00:08:11,116 --> 00:08:12,868
I HAVE SOMETHING IMPORTANT THIS MONTH

108
00:08:12,993 --> 00:08:14,661
CAN YOU SEND IT A WEEK EARLY?

109
00:08:20,042 --> 00:08:22,753
MY DEAR DICTATOR VER. 3

110
00:08:40,729 --> 00:08:42,648
I waited, but I never heard from you.

111
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:47,110
I've done my research,
so I know where you usually show up.

112
00:08:48,737 --> 00:08:51,907
Ahyeon Library,
Hanpung Bookstore, Haneul Park,

113
00:08:52,032 --> 00:08:54,201
Jake Coffee Gongdeok Branch, Nemo's Cafe…

114
00:08:54,326 --> 00:08:55,160
Oh.

115
00:08:55,744 --> 00:08:57,579
Yeoju Auntie's Home-Style Fish Grill.

116
00:08:57,704 --> 00:08:59,081
Wow.

117
00:08:59,206 --> 00:09:01,291
Their charcoal-grilled mackerel is crazy.

118
00:09:05,504 --> 00:09:07,673
You really should sign the settlement.

119
00:09:09,883 --> 00:09:13,553
We'll guarantee
up to 30% of the copyright.

120
00:09:15,055 --> 00:09:15,973
SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT

121
00:09:18,225 --> 00:09:19,142
Are you married?

122
00:09:21,395 --> 00:09:22,562
That's random.

123
00:09:27,859 --> 00:09:29,361
So it wasn't this bastard.

124
00:09:30,070 --> 00:09:30,904
"This bastard"?

125
00:09:47,129 --> 00:09:49,006
Show up like this again, and you're dead.

126
00:09:55,929 --> 00:09:58,056
Your mom owns a building in Yeonhui-dong.

127
00:09:59,933 --> 00:10:02,102
Is that why you're so fearless?

128
00:10:05,897 --> 00:10:08,150
We have to know our opponent well.

129
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:12,362
We call this
a preliminary fact-checking review.

130
00:10:14,531 --> 00:10:16,700
Your older brother runs
a pipe cleaning company.

131
00:10:16,825 --> 00:10:18,744
Your younger brother's
the first Korean diver

132
00:10:18,869 --> 00:10:21,204
to set a record
in the constant weight category.

133
00:10:21,788 --> 00:10:23,957
And your long-time boyfriend…

134
00:10:26,001 --> 00:10:27,711
I know you broke up recently.

135
00:10:31,590 --> 00:10:33,175
Was it because of this?

136
00:10:35,427 --> 00:10:38,013
Wow, what a piece of trash.

137
00:10:38,138 --> 00:10:40,015
What a bastard.

138
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:42,059
You don't abandon someone
during tough times.

139
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:43,894
Right?

140
00:10:47,689 --> 00:10:49,775
We have to know our opponent well.

141
00:10:50,817 --> 00:10:52,194
We call this

142
00:10:53,028 --> 00:10:54,946
a preliminary fact-checking review.

143
00:10:55,072 --> 00:10:57,824
Your older brother runs
a pipe cleaning company…

144
00:10:59,076 --> 00:11:01,453
Unauthorized and unjust background checks.

145
00:11:01,578 --> 00:11:03,330
Illegal interference in mediation.

146
00:11:03,455 --> 00:11:05,415
Threats using my family.

147
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:07,584
Inciting fear under the guise of a deal.

148
00:11:07,709 --> 00:11:10,128
This will be very helpful in court.
Thank you.

149
00:11:11,463 --> 00:11:12,464
Let's add one more.

150
00:11:12,589 --> 00:11:13,840
Property damage.

151
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:31,817
Oh, I'll buy a new phone
and send it to you today.

152
00:11:38,573 --> 00:11:39,616
Ms. Lee.

153
00:11:40,992 --> 00:11:43,120
I'm drowning in work lately.

154
00:11:43,912 --> 00:11:46,581
So I wanted to settle
this trivial case and be done,

155
00:11:46,706 --> 00:11:48,417
which is why I was being nice.

156
00:11:49,584 --> 00:11:51,169
But you're making this difficult.

157
00:11:51,294 --> 00:11:53,964
Since you want it so badly,
I'll see you in court.

158
00:11:54,089 --> 00:11:55,632
You better be fully prepared.

159
00:12:13,567 --> 00:12:14,901
Bill me for it.

160
00:12:15,026 --> 00:12:18,155
Oh, and make sure to send me
the newest phone model.

161
00:12:19,072 --> 00:12:21,450
In white, with 1 terabyte of storage.

162
00:12:42,304 --> 00:12:45,307
I know the reason why
the fourth sample had issues.

163
00:12:45,432 --> 00:12:47,559
Want me to tell you?

164
00:12:53,064 --> 00:12:55,984
See you at Omyeong's Pyongyang
Cold Noodles on the 9th at noon.

165
00:12:57,277 --> 00:12:58,320
I'll tell you then.

166
00:12:59,696 --> 00:13:00,864
Um…

167
00:13:05,076 --> 00:13:06,203
Ouch! Jeez.

168
00:13:07,496 --> 00:13:08,330
What's this?

169
00:13:08,455 --> 00:13:10,040
What are you doing here?

170
00:13:10,832 --> 00:13:13,126
Jeez, you're always so impatient.

171
00:13:13,251 --> 00:13:15,170
Are you here
because of the sample schedule?

172
00:13:15,295 --> 00:13:17,380
Unbelievable, man.

173
00:13:17,506 --> 00:13:19,549
-Jeez.
-We need to talk.

174
00:13:20,133 --> 00:13:20,967
Come on.

175
00:13:22,844 --> 00:13:24,721
You forgot about our appointment.

176
00:13:28,266 --> 00:13:29,100
Oh.

177
00:13:31,102 --> 00:13:34,356
I'm sorry, but I never said I'd go.

178
00:13:35,565 --> 00:13:36,399
Why not?

179
00:13:36,525 --> 00:13:39,194
You wanted to know
why there was a difference in taste

180
00:13:39,319 --> 00:13:40,820
between the lab and factory samples.

181
00:13:40,946 --> 00:13:43,698
I heard you even checked
the sweet potato farms on-site, no?

182
00:13:43,823 --> 00:13:45,909
That's correct, but…

183
00:13:47,118 --> 00:13:50,330
I'm no longer young enough
to get tangled up in a mess.

184
00:13:52,165 --> 00:13:54,292
I may look young, but I'm 35.

185
00:13:56,378 --> 00:13:58,088
-Is that relevant?
-Of course it is.

186
00:13:58,213 --> 00:14:00,674
At 35, your skeletal muscle mass
starts decreasing,

187
00:14:00,799 --> 00:14:04,678
and you're too old to get
the youth and job-seeking allowances.

188
00:14:04,803 --> 00:14:07,514
So you have to take good care of yourself.

189
00:14:07,639 --> 00:14:10,058
Well, simply put,

190
00:14:10,725 --> 00:14:14,020
I want to work here
without any issues until I retire.

191
00:14:14,563 --> 00:14:15,897
That's all.

192
00:14:18,108 --> 00:14:20,694
Some of the sweet potatoes
were swapped with imported ones.

193
00:14:26,533 --> 00:14:27,951
I'll pretend I didn't hear that.

194
00:14:28,577 --> 00:14:29,828
But you did hear it.

195
00:14:34,124 --> 00:14:35,292
I didn't.

196
00:14:40,255 --> 00:14:41,798
I understand what you mean.

197
00:14:42,507 --> 00:14:44,509
I asked too much of the wrong person.

198
00:14:45,552 --> 00:14:46,761
I apologize.

199
00:14:54,477 --> 00:14:56,980
The texture
of the Spicy SweeTato Chips was bad.

200
00:14:57,105 --> 00:14:59,399
And the spicy seasoning
with the sweet potatoes?

201
00:14:59,983 --> 00:15:01,985
It was absolutely the worst.

202
00:15:14,164 --> 00:15:15,915
Right, Mr. Yoon asked

203
00:15:16,041 --> 00:15:18,668
if they could send
the bid market analysis plan tomorrow.

204
00:15:18,793 --> 00:15:20,420
-Tomorrow?
-His place got broken into.

205
00:15:20,545 --> 00:15:22,213
He has to go to the police.

206
00:15:22,339 --> 00:15:23,590
They broke the lock.

207
00:15:23,715 --> 00:15:25,050
The lock?

208
00:15:25,175 --> 00:15:26,134
Yes.

209
00:15:37,103 --> 00:15:38,104
Is it not working?

210
00:15:38,688 --> 00:15:40,023
Is the machine broken?

211
00:15:40,148 --> 00:15:42,901
Why would it be broken?
It worked fine earlier.

212
00:15:45,945 --> 00:15:47,155
What the hell?

213
00:15:47,739 --> 00:15:48,907
What's wrong with this?

214
00:15:52,285 --> 00:15:53,119
Come on.

215
00:16:07,759 --> 00:16:10,512
HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY

216
00:16:13,807 --> 00:16:15,475
It's acting up again.

217
00:16:20,647 --> 00:16:21,731
Come on.

218
00:16:23,108 --> 00:16:24,150
Hey!

219
00:16:26,444 --> 00:16:29,322
Didn't I tell you to get a new one?

220
00:16:29,447 --> 00:16:30,448
Did you?

221
00:16:30,573 --> 00:16:31,991
Many times, in my head.

222
00:16:32,784 --> 00:16:34,077
Get a new one, now.

223
00:17:44,689 --> 00:17:45,523
Um…

224
00:18:08,004 --> 00:18:08,838
HONDURAS KARAOKE

225
00:18:08,963 --> 00:18:10,882
I pushed you away

226
00:18:11,007 --> 00:18:15,637
Only after love has left

227
00:18:15,762 --> 00:18:19,557
Do we realize?

228
00:18:20,099 --> 00:18:25,230
Why did I wander
When you were right beside me?

229
00:18:25,355 --> 00:18:28,650
Now I finally know

230
00:18:29,317 --> 00:18:30,151
The…

231
00:18:30,276 --> 00:18:32,570
Damn it.

232
00:18:34,697 --> 00:18:36,241
I've been thinking.

233
00:18:37,242 --> 00:18:38,993
If you and Ho break up,

234
00:18:39,702 --> 00:18:41,663
I think I'll have to go with him.

235
00:18:41,788 --> 00:18:42,664
Sorry.

236
00:18:45,875 --> 00:18:47,085
You brat.

237
00:18:48,294 --> 00:18:50,797
You'd think Ho gave birth to him.

238
00:18:50,922 --> 00:18:52,173
It's like he's his son.

239
00:18:53,591 --> 00:18:55,301
Yes, he is his son.

240
00:18:55,927 --> 00:18:57,887
Ho raised him since he was two.

241
00:19:06,813 --> 00:19:09,023
Ho and I are done for real.

242
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:11,150
I have zero intention
of getting back together.

243
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:15,697
I don't need your pity, so save it.

244
00:19:15,822 --> 00:19:18,491
Don't flatter yourself, Director.

245
00:19:18,616 --> 00:19:21,536
I'm not here as an old classmate.
I'm here as a producer.

246
00:19:22,328 --> 00:19:25,164
I came to persuade you
about the settlement for the last time,

247
00:19:25,290 --> 00:19:28,084
but you're in no state to talk.

248
00:19:28,209 --> 00:19:30,211
Good luck with the lawsuit.

249
00:19:30,336 --> 00:19:31,588
We'll do our best, too.

250
00:19:37,427 --> 00:19:39,846
And this isn't
as your old classmate or a producer

251
00:19:39,971 --> 00:19:42,223
but just as a fellow human being…

252
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:43,558
Don't say it.

253
00:19:43,683 --> 00:19:46,561
Just get back together with Ho.

254
00:19:53,318 --> 00:19:56,112
I'm never getting back together with him.

255
00:19:59,407 --> 00:20:01,200
I don't want to hate someone anymore.

256
00:20:04,162 --> 00:20:06,289
And I don't want to be hated either.

257
00:20:27,352 --> 00:20:29,062
She's so lazy.

258
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:49,958
She doesn't even care about the fine dust.

259
00:21:01,636 --> 00:21:03,262
She should clean once in a while.

260
00:21:08,977 --> 00:21:10,561
How can someone be so lazy?

261
00:21:14,983 --> 00:21:16,943
She didn't even put away her laundry.

262
00:21:35,253 --> 00:21:36,295
Damn it.

263
00:21:39,007 --> 00:21:40,341
Come on.

264
00:22:04,449 --> 00:22:05,450
Look.

265
00:22:07,076 --> 00:22:08,119
I…

266
00:22:11,039 --> 00:22:12,832
Hey, my charger.

267
00:22:13,583 --> 00:22:16,377
Since we broke up,
you should've given it back.

268
00:23:09,430 --> 00:23:12,892
Namgung-Jerk, you jerk.

269
00:23:41,671 --> 00:23:44,715
SEO JU-HYEOK

270
00:23:51,305 --> 00:23:53,057
Ju-hyeok, I can't--

271
00:23:53,182 --> 00:23:54,100
Ms. Song?

272
00:23:56,185 --> 00:23:57,019
Mr. Han?

273
00:23:57,145 --> 00:23:58,813
Why do you have Ju-hyeok's phone…

274
00:23:59,480 --> 00:24:01,482
I want to talk to Ju-hyeok one last time.

275
00:24:02,024 --> 00:24:03,401
Please, I'm begging you.

276
00:24:03,526 --> 00:24:04,944
No, I'm the one…

277
00:24:08,156 --> 00:24:10,533
who's begging you.

278
00:24:10,658 --> 00:24:12,702
Don't mistake the genre here.

279
00:24:12,827 --> 00:24:16,706
You're in a soap opera about an affair,
but you're acting like it's pure romance.

280
00:24:19,375 --> 00:24:20,543
It's laughable.

281
00:24:20,668 --> 00:24:22,670
I won't let you get away with this.

282
00:24:23,963 --> 00:24:26,674
I won't let this go.

283
00:24:26,799 --> 00:24:28,134
Just in case,

284
00:24:28,259 --> 00:24:30,428
avoid making a scene
this Thursday and Friday.

285
00:24:31,512 --> 00:24:32,722
I'll be busy then.

286
00:24:33,264 --> 00:24:34,640
I'm hanging up now.

287
00:24:34,765 --> 00:24:35,933
SONG HAE-NA

288
00:24:42,023 --> 00:24:44,108
JAEKANG LAW FIRM

289
00:24:45,651 --> 00:24:48,696
The person you are calling is unavailable.
Please leave a message…

290
00:24:58,873 --> 00:25:01,626
Ju-hyeok, I'm not a child.

291
00:25:01,751 --> 00:25:04,378
Don't worry about me
while you're on your business trip.

292
00:25:05,504 --> 00:25:07,965
Take care of your work.
I'll see you next week.

293
00:25:09,842 --> 00:25:10,843
I love you.

294
00:25:13,971 --> 00:25:15,890
That's not your color.

295
00:25:28,611 --> 00:25:32,698
WHEN THAT DAY COMES

296
00:25:32,823 --> 00:25:34,200
ACTRESS SONG HAE-NA

297
00:25:36,494 --> 00:25:38,204
Ms. Song, where are you?

298
00:25:39,705 --> 00:25:40,748
Are you kidding me?

299
00:25:40,873 --> 00:25:44,168
I just slipped something fun
into Ms. Kang's bag.

300
00:25:44,961 --> 00:25:47,713
Photos of Ju-hyeok and me at the hotel.

301
00:25:49,257 --> 00:25:50,132
How fun, right?

302
00:25:52,093 --> 00:25:53,511
Ms. Song.

303
00:25:54,762 --> 00:25:56,264
Don't do something you'll regret.

304
00:25:56,389 --> 00:25:57,765
I'm curious.

305
00:25:58,975 --> 00:26:03,437
I wonder how well Seo Ju-hyeok's lapdog
can clean up his mess.

306
00:26:22,623 --> 00:26:24,667
DIRECTOR LEE MI-DO

307
00:26:31,173 --> 00:26:32,383
Why so quiet?

308
00:26:33,217 --> 00:26:34,427
I'm thinking.

309
00:26:37,346 --> 00:26:39,515
You know, the photos
are already in the cloud.

310
00:26:40,433 --> 00:26:42,727
You shouldn't get any funny ideas.

311
00:26:47,565 --> 00:26:49,317
Why are you talking down to me?

312
00:26:50,443 --> 00:26:52,653
Isn't talking down essential
for a power trip?

313
00:26:57,700 --> 00:26:59,952
First, explain to me what happened.

314
00:27:00,745 --> 00:27:03,456
I spent over three months
pointing a camera at her.

315
00:27:03,581 --> 00:27:05,833
That's not your color.

316
00:27:06,792 --> 00:27:09,628
Even under a scarf and hat,
I recognized her instantly.

317
00:27:17,094 --> 00:27:19,055
Oh my gosh! I'm so sorry.

318
00:27:20,723 --> 00:27:21,974
It's fine. I'll do it.

319
00:27:22,099 --> 00:27:24,685
-Do you have tissues?
-Okay. Oh my goodness.

320
00:27:26,979 --> 00:27:28,230
I'm sorry.

321
00:27:30,399 --> 00:27:33,194
At first, I thought you were the guy
she was seeing.

322
00:27:33,778 --> 00:27:36,572
Your suit, watch, and shoes

323
00:27:37,323 --> 00:27:38,949
are exactly like his.

324
00:27:39,992 --> 00:27:41,702
But you're much more important.

325
00:27:41,827 --> 00:27:43,496
Just tell me what you want.

326
00:27:43,621 --> 00:27:45,706
First of all, apologize.

327
00:27:49,960 --> 00:27:52,546
About breaking your phone--

328
00:27:52,671 --> 00:27:54,465
No, not that.

329
00:27:55,007 --> 00:27:55,883
Oh.

330
00:27:57,051 --> 00:27:58,803
About investigating your family--

331
00:27:58,928 --> 00:28:01,764
He's not trash, and he's not a jerk.

332
00:28:02,640 --> 00:28:04,725
You can't talk about him like that.

333
00:28:07,186 --> 00:28:08,354
Didn't you break up?

334
00:28:08,479 --> 00:28:10,898
Even so, he doesn't deserve all that.

335
00:28:11,565 --> 00:28:14,610
Wow, it must've been true love.

336
00:28:14,735 --> 00:28:17,279
You still care this much
even after breaking up.

337
00:28:17,405 --> 00:28:18,614
Fine, I apologize.

338
00:28:18,739 --> 00:28:19,657
But…

339
00:28:19,782 --> 00:28:22,326
forget the apology.
Tell me what you really want.

340
00:28:22,451 --> 00:28:24,203
Double my current directing fee.

341
00:28:26,372 --> 00:28:28,082
I want a co-director credit

342
00:28:28,207 --> 00:28:30,584
and a guaranteed 50% stake
in the original work.

343
00:28:30,709 --> 00:28:33,170
Oh, and any articles about my departure

344
00:28:33,838 --> 00:28:36,132
must be agreed upon in advance.

345
00:28:37,299 --> 00:28:39,552
A week should be enough time, right?

346
00:28:47,643 --> 00:28:48,644
HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY R&D CENTER

347
00:28:48,769 --> 00:28:49,645
Hey, Sang-hun.

348
00:28:49,770 --> 00:28:52,690
I'm at the Incheon Research Center
for the Snack Department meeting.

349
00:28:53,441 --> 00:28:55,192
Compare the last consumer survey feedback

350
00:28:55,901 --> 00:28:58,112
with the sensory evaluation results
and send them…

351
00:28:58,237 --> 00:29:00,197
Can we talk for a second, please?

352
00:29:01,073 --> 00:29:03,701
Am I the only one
who thinks we have a thing?

353
00:29:04,952 --> 00:29:08,164
We just had a meal to discuss work.
You're overreacting.

354
00:29:08,956 --> 00:29:10,916
You call that just work?

355
00:29:11,041 --> 00:29:12,084
Yes.

356
00:29:13,210 --> 00:29:15,671
You asked me out on a Friday night

357
00:29:15,796 --> 00:29:18,507
just to ask about grub infestations
in sweet potato fields?

358
00:29:18,632 --> 00:29:19,758
Yes.

359
00:29:20,509 --> 00:29:22,386
Since sweet potatoes
are our main ingredient,

360
00:29:22,511 --> 00:29:24,263
I needed to study them in depth.

361
00:29:24,388 --> 00:29:26,265
And you're in charge of root crops,

362
00:29:26,390 --> 00:29:27,641
so I asked your opinion.

363
00:29:27,766 --> 00:29:30,311
Who asks for an opinion on a Friday night?

364
00:29:36,859 --> 00:29:39,069
I have no personal feelings for you.

365
00:29:39,945 --> 00:29:42,198
Please don't contact me
unless it's for work.

366
00:29:42,323 --> 00:29:44,074
You've got to be kidding me.

367
00:29:46,243 --> 00:29:47,620
Damn it.

368
00:29:58,088 --> 00:29:59,673
Can I have one?

369
00:30:02,176 --> 00:30:03,385
These are strong.

370
00:30:03,511 --> 00:30:05,763
I smoke those, too. Raven Blue.

371
00:30:08,265 --> 00:30:11,602
The person who got me smoking
in high school smoked those.

372
00:30:17,483 --> 00:30:18,400
What a psycho.

373
00:30:19,109 --> 00:30:20,945
Getting a high schooler to smoke these?

374
00:30:21,862 --> 00:30:23,197
Let's head to the meeting.

375
00:30:29,578 --> 00:30:33,249
How does it make sense to swap perilla
for sesame in O-SweeTato Chips?

376
00:30:34,959 --> 00:30:38,087
Whether it makes sense or not
isn't the point right now.

377
00:30:38,837 --> 00:30:41,215
The monsoon wiped out the perilla crops.

378
00:30:41,340 --> 00:30:43,342
We had no choice. Besides,

379
00:30:44,426 --> 00:30:47,263
the Research Team approved
using sesame instead.

380
00:30:49,515 --> 00:30:52,851
The board meeting is in two days.
We can't do a tasting this way.

381
00:30:56,397 --> 00:30:59,066
What does everyone else think?

382
00:30:59,191 --> 00:31:00,484
Do you agree with her?

383
00:31:03,279 --> 00:31:04,613
I can't really tell.

384
00:31:05,614 --> 00:31:06,657
It tastes the same.

385
00:31:06,782 --> 00:31:08,701
-It's fine.
-Yes.

386
00:31:10,244 --> 00:31:12,288
See that, Ms. Park?

387
00:31:12,413 --> 00:31:14,832
Most people can't tell the difference.

388
00:31:14,957 --> 00:31:16,166
Why don't you drop it?

389
00:31:17,668 --> 00:31:19,962
There's definitely an acidic aftertaste.

390
00:31:21,380 --> 00:31:24,091
Since sesame has
a high unsaturated fat content,

391
00:31:24,216 --> 00:31:25,175
it goes rancid faster,

392
00:31:25,968 --> 00:31:28,387
which seems to ruin the aftertaste.

393
00:31:28,512 --> 00:31:30,472
If there's an issue with the ingredients,

394
00:31:30,598 --> 00:31:33,142
I hope we can work things out
through discussion.

395
00:31:33,767 --> 00:31:35,311
If the mix ratio changes,

396
00:31:35,436 --> 00:31:38,314
we'll share the data with Purchasing first

397
00:31:38,439 --> 00:31:39,940
and ask if it's okay.

398
00:31:40,065 --> 00:31:41,442
All right, understood.

399
00:31:42,443 --> 00:31:44,570
We'll do that from now on.

400
00:31:45,279 --> 00:31:47,364
Let's let it slide
for the upcoming board meeting.

401
00:31:47,489 --> 00:31:49,783
We can't make new seasoning now.

402
00:31:49,908 --> 00:31:51,452
I'll make it.

403
00:32:13,599 --> 00:32:14,850
Please, just say it.

404
00:32:15,601 --> 00:32:17,061
About the imported sweet potatoes,

405
00:32:17,186 --> 00:32:19,563
did you report to Manager Yoon
in Snack Team 4?

406
00:32:23,108 --> 00:32:24,360
I didn't.

407
00:32:25,110 --> 00:32:27,363
If you can't trust your direct superior,

408
00:32:27,488 --> 00:32:29,406
you could have reported it to Audit.

409
00:32:33,702 --> 00:32:35,329
Too many people are involved.

410
00:32:35,454 --> 00:32:37,706
Without direct evidence,

411
00:32:37,831 --> 00:32:40,042
like the Distribution Team bribery case,

412
00:32:40,167 --> 00:32:42,127
they'd only punish a few pawns.

413
00:32:43,420 --> 00:32:46,507
Were you trying to drag me
into something so obviously risky?

414
00:32:46,632 --> 00:32:48,342
I'm a bit selfish.

415
00:32:49,218 --> 00:32:50,386
I couldn't do it alone.

416
00:33:00,437 --> 00:33:01,814
Among the people involved,

417
00:33:01,939 --> 00:33:04,441
is there anyone you have a history with?

418
00:33:04,566 --> 00:33:07,403
For example, a secret blood relative?

419
00:33:07,528 --> 00:33:09,571
Or maybe a feud between families?

420
00:33:09,697 --> 00:33:11,949
Are you seeking revenge with this?

421
00:33:12,074 --> 00:33:13,492
Is that your motivation?

422
00:33:14,660 --> 00:33:17,496
Sorry to disappoint,
but there's nothing like that involved.

423
00:33:21,709 --> 00:33:24,712
Are you trying to be
the youngest Assistant Manager,

424
00:33:24,837 --> 00:33:26,755
-then an executive--
-No, I'm not.

425
00:33:30,259 --> 00:33:31,802
So you're doing this for nothing?

426
00:33:32,928 --> 00:33:33,929
That's ridiculous.

427
00:33:36,098 --> 00:33:37,141
It's just my nature.

428
00:33:38,183 --> 00:33:39,727
I can't ignore what I've seen.

429
00:33:39,852 --> 00:33:42,479
Once I'm fixated,
I have to resolve all my doubts.

430
00:33:42,604 --> 00:33:44,606
I can't help but keep digging.

431
00:33:45,315 --> 00:33:47,943
It's not out of
a sense of justice or duty.

432
00:33:48,068 --> 00:33:51,238
I just have a difficult personality.

433
00:33:54,032 --> 00:33:55,993
Okay, I understand.

434
00:33:56,118 --> 00:33:58,829
Since you're so determined,
I'll respect that.

435
00:34:06,378 --> 00:34:08,422
You've heard about Kitchen Lab 3, right?

436
00:34:10,632 --> 00:34:11,759
Oh, you didn't?

437
00:34:11,884 --> 00:34:14,762
You shouldn't be here alone.

438
00:34:15,345 --> 00:34:17,222
It's known to be haunted by a ghost.

439
00:34:17,347 --> 00:34:18,557
It's not just a rumor.

440
00:34:18,682 --> 00:34:20,142
I saw it while working here.

441
00:34:20,267 --> 00:34:21,894
I don't care.

442
00:34:22,019 --> 00:34:22,936
I can beat it.

443
00:34:23,061 --> 00:34:24,938
Wow.

444
00:34:29,443 --> 00:34:31,403
Say hi for me if you see it.

445
00:34:32,946 --> 00:34:34,239
Ask how it's doing.

446
00:34:34,364 --> 00:34:36,033
Yes, I will.

447
00:34:54,760 --> 00:34:55,761
Hey.

448
00:35:01,016 --> 00:35:02,309
CONTEST FOR ENGAGED COUPLES

449
00:35:04,353 --> 00:35:05,187
So,

450
00:35:05,312 --> 00:35:08,565
I heard a wedding hall
was hosting an event for engaged couples,

451
00:35:08,690 --> 00:35:10,317
so I signed you two up.

452
00:35:11,652 --> 00:35:12,653
If you guys enter,

453
00:35:12,778 --> 00:35:15,030
-you'll definitely win first place.
-First place!

454
00:35:16,031 --> 00:35:17,866
Even fifth place gets red ginseng.

455
00:35:18,534 --> 00:35:19,368
You know?

456
00:35:19,493 --> 00:35:22,538
Newlyweds are tired day and night.

457
00:35:22,663 --> 00:35:24,957
Red ginseng is the best choice for energy.

458
00:35:25,082 --> 00:35:26,750
-Red ginseng is the best!
-Right.

459
00:35:29,837 --> 00:35:32,130
Okay, how about fourth place?

460
00:35:32,256 --> 00:35:33,841
A Bellafino coffee machine.

461
00:35:33,966 --> 00:35:35,759
The crema is amazing!

462
00:35:35,884 --> 00:35:38,554
Imagine having a delicious espresso
every morning.

463
00:35:38,679 --> 00:35:41,473
-Yes. Mi-do, you like coffee, right?
-You love it.

464
00:35:43,350 --> 00:35:46,895
Third place gets
a 20-liter Humiel dehumidifier.

465
00:35:47,020 --> 00:35:48,856
It's amazing in the rainy season.

466
00:35:48,981 --> 00:35:50,899
You won't even know it's raining.

467
00:35:51,024 --> 00:35:52,401
So soft and dry.

468
00:35:54,987 --> 00:35:56,446
Second place, Airponic Dress Care.

469
00:35:56,572 --> 00:35:57,948
You always wear dress shirts.

470
00:35:58,073 --> 00:36:00,576
The collars get dirty.
You can't wash them every day.

471
00:36:04,246 --> 00:36:07,082
For first place, a LaRobot robot vacuum.

472
00:36:08,709 --> 00:36:11,086
The top model
with self-navigation and mopping.

473
00:36:13,297 --> 00:36:14,256
Oh?

474
00:36:14,381 --> 00:36:16,758
-What do you think?
-A robot vacuum.

475
00:36:16,884 --> 00:36:19,553
It does it all,
mopping and self-navigation.

476
00:36:20,262 --> 00:36:21,680
-A robot vacuum.
-Mi-do.

477
00:36:22,347 --> 00:36:25,309
You don't even need first place.
Even fifth gets red ginseng.

478
00:36:27,311 --> 00:36:28,270
Now, let's begin

479
00:36:28,395 --> 00:36:32,065
the contest for engaged couples!

480
00:36:32,190 --> 00:36:35,736
Let's start with a big round
of applause and cheers!

481
00:36:36,570 --> 00:36:38,071
BUSINESS COUPLE

482
00:36:38,196 --> 00:36:39,531
Everyone, cheer them on!

483
00:36:39,656 --> 00:36:41,241
-Good luck!
-Good luck!

484
00:36:43,452 --> 00:36:44,870
We split it 50-50.

485
00:36:45,704 --> 00:36:47,497
-Don't change your mind later.
-You too.

486
00:36:47,623 --> 00:36:49,666
We have incredible prizes lined up.

487
00:36:51,877 --> 00:36:53,003
TELEPATHY

488
00:36:53,128 --> 00:36:54,212
Now, the first question.

489
00:36:54,338 --> 00:36:57,841
In the morning,
what website does your boyfriend visit

490
00:36:57,966 --> 00:36:59,801
as soon as he wakes up?

491
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:04,431
Three, two, one.

492
00:37:04,556 --> 00:37:06,016
Please show your answers.

493
00:37:06,141 --> 00:37:08,018
TODAY'S DEALS

494
00:37:08,143 --> 00:37:09,186
Wow!

495
00:37:09,311 --> 00:37:11,146
-That's right! Nice!
-Nice!

496
00:37:11,271 --> 00:37:13,190
-All right!
-You knew it!

497
00:37:13,315 --> 00:37:17,152
What is your girlfriend's
weirdest sleeping habit?

498
00:37:17,945 --> 00:37:19,196
Hold them up.

499
00:37:19,321 --> 00:37:21,073
DOING A FULL 360

500
00:37:21,239 --> 00:37:22,449
All right, awesome!

501
00:37:22,574 --> 00:37:26,161
What is your go-to karaoke song?

502
00:37:28,914 --> 00:37:30,791
-That's it!
-Okay!

503
00:37:30,916 --> 00:37:31,792
A THOUSAND-YEAR LOVE

504
00:37:31,917 --> 00:37:33,377
-Nice!
-They knew it!

505
00:37:33,502 --> 00:37:34,378
SPEED QUIZ

506
00:37:34,503 --> 00:37:35,379
KEYWORD: BICYCLE

507
00:37:36,046 --> 00:37:37,923
I gave you this for our fifth anniversary.

508
00:37:38,048 --> 00:37:40,175
You lost it in a week, and we fought.

509
00:37:40,300 --> 00:37:41,385
Necklace!

510
00:37:41,927 --> 00:37:43,929
That was our third. Think of our fifth.

511
00:37:44,054 --> 00:37:46,098
Oh, when you were in second grade,

512
00:37:46,223 --> 00:37:47,641
this made you break your leg.

513
00:37:47,766 --> 00:37:50,102
-I carried you to school for days.
-Bicycle?

514
00:37:50,227 --> 00:37:51,061
Yes!

515
00:37:51,812 --> 00:37:54,272
Oh! The person you hate most in the world.

516
00:37:54,398 --> 00:37:55,232
Lee Yeong-do!

517
00:37:55,357 --> 00:37:56,817
But another word for him.

518
00:37:56,942 --> 00:37:57,901
-Parasite!
-Not that.

519
00:37:58,026 --> 00:38:01,571
Scumbag, psychopath, total jerk,
a future lonely old man!

520
00:38:01,697 --> 00:38:02,990
Not any of that.

521
00:38:04,324 --> 00:38:08,161
You said you'd rather bite your tongue off
than call him this.

522
00:38:08,286 --> 00:38:09,538
Oppa!

523
00:38:09,663 --> 00:38:10,580
KEYWORD: OPPA

524
00:38:10,706 --> 00:38:12,582
-All right!
-Yes!

525
00:38:15,961 --> 00:38:16,920
TELEPATHY ORIGAMI

526
00:38:17,087 --> 00:38:18,797
Fold it up first,
so the corner touches the top.

527
00:38:18,922 --> 00:38:19,756
-Okay.
-Okay.

528
00:38:19,881 --> 00:38:22,592
Fold both sides to the center,
forming a triangle.

529
00:38:22,718 --> 00:38:23,552
-Okay.
-Next.

530
00:38:23,677 --> 00:38:25,303
Fold the top and both ends back.

531
00:38:25,429 --> 00:38:26,638
-Okay.
-Okay.

532
00:38:26,763 --> 00:38:27,639
Ta-da!

533
00:38:30,100 --> 00:38:32,310
Now, we only have the final game left.

534
00:38:32,436 --> 00:38:33,937
1ST: BUSINESS COUPLE, 520 POINTS

535
00:38:34,062 --> 00:38:35,731
This game is a heart rate test.

536
00:38:36,481 --> 00:38:39,151
It's called "Steal My Heart."

537
00:38:39,276 --> 00:38:42,487
You can turn the tables with this game.

538
00:38:42,612 --> 00:38:47,534
Because the sum of your heart rates

539
00:38:47,659 --> 00:38:49,619
will be your score.

540
00:38:49,745 --> 00:38:51,538
The time limit is one minute.

541
00:38:51,663 --> 00:38:53,707
Let's begin!

542
00:38:54,332 --> 00:38:55,417
-Let's go!
-All right.

543
00:38:55,542 --> 00:38:59,963
I love how the couples
are looking into each other's eyes.

544
00:39:00,088 --> 00:39:02,716
-Hey, they're going up.
-They're going up!

545
00:39:03,550 --> 00:39:07,679
-The numbers don't lie in this game.
-There we go!

546
00:39:07,804 --> 00:39:09,473
-The Heart-stopper Couple's heart rates…
-It's working!

547
00:39:09,598 --> 00:39:11,391
-… are already rising.
-I didn't think it would.

548
00:39:11,516 --> 00:39:14,853
-I thought their feelings had dried up.
-Their hearts are pounding right now!

549
00:39:16,480 --> 00:39:17,314
BUSINESS COUPLE
M 99, F 90

550
00:39:17,439 --> 00:39:19,858
-What?
-What's going on with the Business Couple?

551
00:39:19,983 --> 00:39:22,277
Their numbers suddenly started to drop.

552
00:39:22,903 --> 00:39:26,740
They were way ahead until just now.

553
00:39:26,865 --> 00:39:29,868
They're way too calm right now.

554
00:39:44,466 --> 00:39:46,259
-Welcome.
-Hi.

555
00:39:47,761 --> 00:39:49,262
Grab your promotional item.

556
00:39:49,387 --> 00:39:51,264
You get a free item. Hot Chocolate Chips.

557
00:39:52,390 --> 00:39:55,185
When these first came out,
everyone went crazy.

558
00:39:55,310 --> 00:39:58,021
Now, we give them out as freebies.

559
00:40:15,789 --> 00:40:19,501
You might not believe it,
but we were once like that, too.

560
00:40:20,544 --> 00:40:23,046
Every moment was passionate
and made our hearts flutter.

561
00:40:23,880 --> 00:40:26,299
We only had eyes for each other.

562
00:40:27,717 --> 00:40:29,845
Those were the most sparkling days
of our love.

563
00:40:29,970 --> 00:40:30,846
WHEN THAT DAY COMES

564
00:40:32,973 --> 00:40:35,100
Director Bong Joon-ho's film  Parasite

565
00:40:35,225 --> 00:40:39,187
surpassed ten million viewers
in just 53 days after its release.

566
00:40:39,771 --> 00:40:42,566
The film is demonstrating
its cinematic quality and mass appeal

567
00:40:42,691 --> 00:40:45,819
as it breaks both domestic
and international box office records.

568
00:40:45,944 --> 00:40:47,154
WHEN THAT DAY COMES
MI-DO

569
00:40:47,279 --> 00:40:50,282
It's made another major mark
in Korean film history.

570
00:40:53,118 --> 00:40:55,287
I'll come visit you every weekend.

571
00:40:56,204 --> 00:40:57,372
Actually, no.

572
00:40:57,497 --> 00:40:59,499
I'll come every Friday night after work.

573
00:40:59,624 --> 00:41:00,458
No.

574
00:41:00,584 --> 00:41:02,878
It's a ten-hour round trip.
You'll be too tired.

575
00:41:06,381 --> 00:41:07,799
You've changed.

576
00:41:08,466 --> 00:41:11,386
-Won't you miss me?
-I'm just worried about you getting tired.

577
00:41:12,512 --> 00:41:13,805
No, you've changed.

578
00:41:14,764 --> 00:41:17,058
Whenever I call you and ask you something,

579
00:41:17,184 --> 00:41:19,186
you just go, "Uh-huh."

580
00:41:20,270 --> 00:41:22,439
What do you mean?

581
00:41:22,564 --> 00:41:25,567
Of course I go, "Uh-huh."
What else would I say?

582
00:41:26,234 --> 00:41:27,068
It used to be,

583
00:41:27,736 --> 00:41:30,488
"Mm-hmm," remember?

584
00:41:30,614 --> 00:41:34,367
When did I ever go, "Mm-hmm"?

585
00:41:36,244 --> 00:41:38,121
It was like, "Mm-hmm."

586
00:41:40,081 --> 00:41:41,249
Do it again.

587
00:41:42,500 --> 00:41:43,835
Mm-hmm.

588
00:41:44,961 --> 00:41:47,005
-Again.
-Stop it.

589
00:41:47,130 --> 00:41:48,340
Okay.

590
00:41:50,342 --> 00:41:51,593
Seriously.

591
00:41:53,053 --> 00:41:55,013
Yes, the place is nice.

592
00:41:55,138 --> 00:41:57,265
It's better with four of us in the room.

593
00:41:57,390 --> 00:41:58,725
That's a relief.

594
00:42:00,101 --> 00:42:02,312
I miss you already. What do I do?

595
00:42:03,355 --> 00:42:04,648
Should I send a selfie?

596
00:42:04,773 --> 00:42:06,733
No, selfies aren't the real you.

597
00:42:07,567 --> 00:42:08,777
Hey.

598
00:42:12,113 --> 00:42:13,865
How can I wait until the weekend?

599
00:42:15,700 --> 00:42:17,744
By working hard.

600
00:42:19,746 --> 00:42:20,914
I'll call you later.

601
00:42:21,539 --> 00:42:24,876
Are you allowed to call your girlfriend
while waiting for the potatoes?

602
00:42:26,419 --> 00:42:27,545
I'm sorry.

603
00:42:28,505 --> 00:42:32,175
I've finished the seasoning.
I just need to mix it with the potatoes.

604
00:42:42,686 --> 00:42:43,812
Damn it.

605
00:43:24,853 --> 00:43:25,770
That scared me.

606
00:43:36,489 --> 00:43:38,700
Namgung!

607
00:43:49,586 --> 00:43:52,464
What? No reaction?

608
00:43:53,423 --> 00:43:55,842
Aren't you happy to see me?

609
00:43:58,678 --> 00:44:00,847
What happened? What about your shoot?

610
00:44:00,972 --> 00:44:02,849
It got canceled because of the rain.

611
00:44:02,974 --> 00:44:05,226
I caught a ride with someone
heading to Incheon.

612
00:44:06,519 --> 00:44:07,687
How did you get in?

613
00:44:10,106 --> 00:44:12,901
Ta-da! He ran away when he saw me.

614
00:44:15,820 --> 00:44:17,238
We were short on extras today.

615
00:44:17,364 --> 00:44:19,991
The crew had to fill in.
That's why I'm in this.

616
00:44:23,912 --> 00:44:26,831
What's with this boring reaction?

617
00:44:28,583 --> 00:44:29,793
Should I just leave?

618
00:44:31,378 --> 00:44:33,713
I'm leaving. I really am.

619
00:44:33,838 --> 00:44:34,756
Well?

620
00:44:35,965 --> 00:44:37,509
Wow, that's cold.

621
00:44:40,845 --> 00:44:42,389
You're so dead.

622
00:44:44,099 --> 00:44:45,975
You can't be making
these surprise visits, can you?

623
00:44:46,101 --> 00:44:47,394
No.

624
00:44:48,311 --> 00:44:51,606
Your reaction was so weak.
I never want to do it again.

625
00:44:54,359 --> 00:44:55,360
You're in trouble.

626
00:44:57,320 --> 00:44:59,406
What's with the boring reaction?

627
00:44:59,531 --> 00:45:01,324
Such a buzzkill.

628
00:45:02,075 --> 00:45:04,327
You need to react so I can--

629
00:45:50,206 --> 00:45:51,833
-Wait.
-What do we do?

630
00:45:55,253 --> 00:45:58,173
-Oh, Mr. Eom. You're still here.
-Yes.

631
00:45:58,298 --> 00:46:00,467
Well, I was leaving, then…

632
00:46:00,592 --> 00:46:02,343
How about we leave together?

633
00:46:02,469 --> 00:46:03,970
Let's clock out.

634
00:46:04,095 --> 00:46:06,347
But I haven't finished mixing yet.

635
00:46:06,473 --> 00:46:08,266
What?

636
00:46:08,391 --> 00:46:11,561
Come on, you should've
finished this earlier.

637
00:46:12,770 --> 00:46:14,397
Hold on. What?

638
00:46:15,231 --> 00:46:17,901
Why is the color like this?

639
00:46:18,735 --> 00:46:19,903
What is this?

640
00:46:20,028 --> 00:46:23,198
Did you mix dark chocolate and capsaicin?

641
00:46:24,199 --> 00:46:26,493
Yes, when I tasted them separately,

642
00:46:26,618 --> 00:46:29,245
they were too boring, so I tried this.

643
00:46:29,370 --> 00:46:30,997
Come on, really?

644
00:46:31,122 --> 00:46:33,625
Dark chocolate and capsaicin together?

645
00:46:33,750 --> 00:46:35,251
That can't be… What?

646
00:46:35,919 --> 00:46:36,878
Why is this good?

647
00:46:37,003 --> 00:46:38,171
Sorry?

648
00:46:38,296 --> 00:46:39,714
Why does it work?

649
00:46:39,839 --> 00:46:41,424
Wow, it's interesting.

650
00:46:42,884 --> 00:46:44,093
Here, try it.

651
00:46:44,219 --> 00:46:45,261
It's like

652
00:46:45,887 --> 00:46:48,389
the sweetness embraces the spiciness,

653
00:46:48,515 --> 00:46:50,642
neutralizing and softening it.

654
00:46:50,767 --> 00:46:51,851
Mm.

655
00:46:57,315 --> 00:46:58,733
What… Who is that?

656
00:46:59,776 --> 00:47:01,152
Who? Where?

657
00:47:01,277 --> 00:47:03,571
Over there, right there.

658
00:47:04,822 --> 00:47:07,075
Right by the window.

659
00:47:07,200 --> 00:47:09,994
The spirited lady.

660
00:47:11,371 --> 00:47:13,373
By the window? Where…

661
00:47:13,498 --> 00:47:15,416
Right there! Can't you see her?

662
00:47:16,292 --> 00:47:20,046
The lady in the black skirt
and traditional white top.

663
00:47:21,089 --> 00:47:22,423
There's nobody there.

664
00:47:23,091 --> 00:47:24,801
What do you mean? She's right there!

665
00:47:26,010 --> 00:47:29,472
She's smiling at us, right there!

666
00:47:32,976 --> 00:47:34,894
I'm going to head out first.

667
00:47:35,019 --> 00:47:36,729
-I'll just…
-Um…

668
00:47:44,320 --> 00:47:45,488
Will he be okay?

669
00:47:46,656 --> 00:47:49,075
He's stronger than he looks.
He's the toughest mentally.

670
00:47:50,118 --> 00:47:51,619
-Mi-do, try this.
-What?

671
00:47:57,584 --> 00:47:59,043
What? This is crazy.

672
00:47:59,168 --> 00:48:01,546
-Is it good?
-Yes, it's delicious.

673
00:48:02,171 --> 00:48:03,798
Why is it so good?

674
00:48:11,639 --> 00:48:12,473
What's wrong?

675
00:48:13,391 --> 00:48:14,434
Did you cry today?

676
00:48:14,559 --> 00:48:16,686
What are you talking about?

677
00:48:18,062 --> 00:48:20,356
Come on, what happened?

678
00:48:21,858 --> 00:48:23,276
What do you mean?

679
00:48:23,401 --> 00:48:25,862
The shoot got canceled
because of the rain.

680
00:48:25,987 --> 00:48:28,906
I'm so happy. I was excited to see you.

681
00:48:32,327 --> 00:48:33,453
What happened?

682
00:48:34,537 --> 00:48:35,496
Tell me.

683
00:48:46,466 --> 00:48:50,094
The assistant director…

684
00:48:50,219 --> 00:48:51,512
He always does that.

685
00:48:51,638 --> 00:48:54,682
What? What a crazy bastard.

686
00:48:54,807 --> 00:48:56,059
So?

687
00:49:01,731 --> 00:49:04,150
You should've said it wasn't you.

688
00:49:04,275 --> 00:49:06,277
If you quit now, they'll blame you.

689
00:49:13,368 --> 00:49:14,535
Is that jerk on set?

690
00:49:14,661 --> 00:49:18,581
-I'll get this jerk…
-Then I'll die of embarrassment.

691
00:49:20,416 --> 00:49:23,461
Right, if I cause a scene,
you'll look like a fool.

692
00:49:23,586 --> 00:49:26,047
But staying quiet
makes you look like a fool, too.

693
00:49:27,840 --> 00:49:29,759
Even if you quit,

694
00:49:30,343 --> 00:49:32,053
you should speak up first.

695
00:49:35,431 --> 00:49:38,267
Running away like this isn't like you.

696
00:49:40,144 --> 00:49:42,105
Let's go together.

697
00:49:47,151 --> 00:49:48,194
What do we do?

698
00:49:48,319 --> 00:49:50,822
They say there's no way
we'll get 500 people by tomorrow.

699
00:49:50,947 --> 00:49:53,157
Our shoot overlaps
with  Sonata of the Wind.

700
00:49:55,076 --> 00:49:58,496
The schedule clearly said the 28th.

701
00:49:58,621 --> 00:50:01,958
Wasn't that the old schedule?

702
00:50:02,083 --> 00:50:04,752
-What was that, punk?
-I mean…

703
00:50:05,420 --> 00:50:07,547
-I think so.
-Did you mess up again?

704
00:50:10,216 --> 00:50:11,467
Why are you here?

705
00:50:11,592 --> 00:50:13,010
What will you do?

706
00:50:13,136 --> 00:50:14,929
No one left to blame anymore?

707
00:50:17,348 --> 00:50:18,391
Don't worry.

708
00:50:18,516 --> 00:50:21,185
I'm not here to tattle on you
for blaming me

709
00:50:21,310 --> 00:50:23,813
after you ordered the set to be torn down.

710
00:50:25,022 --> 00:50:27,525
What are you talking about?

711
00:50:27,650 --> 00:50:28,985
Are you crazy?

712
00:50:30,361 --> 00:50:31,320
You know what?

713
00:50:32,029 --> 00:50:33,740
You'll never debut as a director.

714
00:50:35,158 --> 00:50:36,909
I saw your short film.

715
00:50:37,034 --> 00:50:39,662
I finally understood why you act this way.

716
00:50:40,538 --> 00:50:44,417
I see now. An inferiority complex
really eats away at you.

717
00:50:44,542 --> 00:50:46,627
I'll never be like that.

718
00:50:46,753 --> 00:50:50,423
Stealing angles and storyboards
and losing my identity.

719
00:50:51,466 --> 00:50:54,761
Becoming a fossil chasing after
premiere after-parties.

720
00:50:57,138 --> 00:50:58,097
Thank you.

721
00:50:58,222 --> 00:51:00,808
Thanks to you, I'll be a great director.

722
00:51:03,478 --> 00:51:04,979
What is she talking about?

723
00:51:05,104 --> 00:51:06,481
What did you just say?

724
00:51:06,606 --> 00:51:08,858
-What did you say? Let go!
-Sir.

725
00:51:08,983 --> 00:51:11,110
-Please calm down.
-Are you out of your mind?

726
00:51:11,235 --> 00:51:13,070
-Wow, that little…
-Calm down.

727
00:51:17,617 --> 00:51:21,370
It was an honor working with you.

728
00:51:26,167 --> 00:51:27,043
Five hundred people.

729
00:51:28,836 --> 00:51:29,754
Excuse me?

730
00:51:29,879 --> 00:51:33,007
If you can get 500 people by tomorrow,

731
00:51:33,132 --> 00:51:36,302
you're the assistant director
of this production.

732
00:51:38,262 --> 00:51:40,306
So, can you do it?

733
00:51:45,436 --> 00:51:47,104
Okay, ready!

734
00:51:47,230 --> 00:51:48,815
-Action!
-Go!

735
00:52:39,907 --> 00:52:41,200
How did you know?

736
00:52:43,870 --> 00:52:46,122
Since we were young, you've always known

737
00:52:47,081 --> 00:52:48,666
when I've been crying.

738
00:52:50,668 --> 00:52:53,004
Even my mother wouldn't notice.

739
00:52:54,338 --> 00:52:55,756
But you always knew.

740
00:52:58,092 --> 00:52:59,260
Come to think of it…

741
00:53:01,095 --> 00:53:02,305
how did I know?

742
00:53:06,142 --> 00:53:07,310
I could just tell.

743
00:53:08,853 --> 00:53:10,521
When you were sad.

744
00:53:18,863 --> 00:53:20,990
Okay, cut!

745
00:53:21,574 --> 00:53:22,575
Cut!

746
00:53:25,494 --> 00:53:26,662
What are they doing?

747
00:53:28,331 --> 00:53:29,707
What?

748
00:53:41,844 --> 00:53:44,013
Hey! Lee Mi-do!

749
00:53:44,138 --> 00:53:45,264
I said cut!

750
00:53:45,389 --> 00:53:47,224
They're crazy, damn it.

751
00:53:48,017 --> 00:53:48,976
What?

752
00:53:49,101 --> 00:53:52,438
Cut, I said cut!

753
00:53:52,563 --> 00:53:55,524
Cut! She's too excited.

754
00:53:55,650 --> 00:53:57,485
-Look. Hey…
-Sir!

755
00:53:57,610 --> 00:53:58,653
Hey!

756
00:53:58,778 --> 00:54:01,572
Hey, stop… It's all blowing up!

757
00:54:01,697 --> 00:54:03,407
Why are you stopping me?

758
00:54:03,532 --> 00:54:05,826
You should stop them! Everything blew up!

759
00:54:08,871 --> 00:54:12,333
Our movie became the year's biggest hit.

760
00:54:12,458 --> 00:54:13,417
SOLD OUT

761
00:54:13,542 --> 00:54:15,211
Oh Gyeong-su's  When That Day Comes

762
00:54:15,336 --> 00:54:17,046
surpassed ten million viewers today,

763
00:54:17,171 --> 00:54:20,508
becoming the year's top film.

764
00:54:22,259 --> 00:54:24,929
The snack we made
was launched as Hot Chocolate Chips.

765
00:54:25,054 --> 00:54:26,222
HOT CHOCOLATE CHIPS SOLD OUT

766
00:54:26,347 --> 00:54:28,057
It always sold out instantly,

767
00:54:28,182 --> 00:54:30,851
causing an unprecedented shopping frenzy.

768
00:54:30,977 --> 00:54:34,230
It made 30 billion won in three months,

769
00:54:34,355 --> 00:54:36,857
and Hunmin Confectionery's stock
rose 60% to a record high.

770
00:54:36,983 --> 00:54:38,150
HOT CHOCOLATE CHIPS SOLD OUT

771
00:54:39,652 --> 00:54:44,281
And our love was
also hitting an all-time high.

772
00:55:35,833 --> 00:55:38,335
The passion we had back then…

773
00:55:38,461 --> 00:55:39,670
the butterflies…

774
00:55:40,629 --> 00:55:42,256
where did it all go?

775
00:55:43,382 --> 00:55:45,509
When did we lose it all?

776
00:56:44,860 --> 00:56:46,070
Are you crazy?

777
00:56:56,622 --> 00:56:57,706
Did you cry today?

778
00:57:00,459 --> 00:57:01,836
Why were you crying?

779
00:57:03,504 --> 00:57:05,172
What happened this time?

780
00:57:05,297 --> 00:57:06,841
Why do you make me…

781
00:57:08,467 --> 00:57:10,970
worry so much about you?

782
00:57:13,180 --> 00:57:14,014
Lee Mi-do?

783
00:57:17,810 --> 00:57:20,396
Wow, how long has it been?

784
00:57:20,521 --> 00:57:22,898
I almost didn't recognize you.

785
00:57:24,400 --> 00:57:25,442
How have you been?

786
00:57:27,111 --> 00:57:29,738
I've been well. And you?

787
00:57:29,864 --> 00:57:31,448
I've been crazy busy, as usual.

788
00:57:31,574 --> 00:57:34,493
Are you here for my premiere?

789
00:57:37,788 --> 00:57:39,165
THE UNINVITED GUEST

790
00:57:39,999 --> 00:57:41,167
Oh, say hello.

791
00:57:41,292 --> 00:57:42,418
Our studio's CEO…

792
00:57:42,543 --> 00:57:43,669
INFINITE RUSH
NA SEUNG-HO

793
00:57:43,794 --> 00:57:45,171
…and the investment firm employees.

794
00:57:46,463 --> 00:57:47,339
Hello.

795
00:57:47,464 --> 00:57:48,966
This is Director Lee Mi-do.

796
00:57:49,091 --> 00:57:50,551
I'm sure you all know her.

797
00:57:50,676 --> 00:57:52,595
After Spring Comes Winter,
The 13th Season…

798
00:57:52,720 --> 00:57:54,305
-You've mentioned her before.
-Right.

799
00:57:58,100 --> 00:57:59,518
Anyway, Director Lee.

800
00:58:00,102 --> 00:58:01,854
Isn't life so funny?

801
00:58:04,064 --> 00:58:05,774
You used to tell me

802
00:58:05,900 --> 00:58:08,402
that I'd never debut as a director.

803
00:58:09,195 --> 00:58:11,572
But the one who never made
their feature film debut

804
00:58:11,697 --> 00:58:13,157
is you.

805
00:58:13,866 --> 00:58:15,951
Remember what you said to me back then?

806
00:58:16,660 --> 00:58:18,787
I'd like to return the favor now.

807
00:58:19,663 --> 00:58:20,706
Director Lee.

808
00:58:20,831 --> 00:58:24,501
You will never make
your feature film debut.

809
00:58:25,878 --> 00:58:29,006
You've lost your drive
and become stagnant.

810
00:58:29,882 --> 00:58:31,217
The only thing left

811
00:58:31,342 --> 00:58:33,802
is to rot away.

812
00:58:35,262 --> 00:58:36,305
Don't you think?

813
00:58:37,932 --> 00:58:38,891
Enjoy the movie.

814
00:58:45,272 --> 00:58:47,358
It has nothing to do with you now.

815
00:58:47,983 --> 00:58:49,193
Just don't worry about it!

816
00:58:49,318 --> 00:58:51,028
I wish I could do that!

817
00:58:52,196 --> 00:58:53,989
I don't want to care, either.

818
00:58:56,116 --> 00:58:57,660
But I can't help it.

819
00:58:57,785 --> 00:58:58,994
You saw what happened.

820
00:58:59,578 --> 00:59:00,746
We're over.

821
00:59:04,333 --> 00:59:05,459
Mi-do.

822
00:59:07,586 --> 00:59:08,712
Let's try.

823
00:59:11,757 --> 00:59:12,716
If we try--

824
00:59:12,841 --> 00:59:14,260
If I could…

825
00:59:15,511 --> 00:59:19,765
I'd warm us up in the microwave
for just 90 seconds.

826
00:59:19,890 --> 00:59:22,768
I want to go back
to when you were all I needed.

827
00:59:23,519 --> 00:59:25,437
But we can't go back.

828
00:59:28,816 --> 00:59:29,692
Namgung.

829
00:59:31,777 --> 00:59:33,696
Do you want to know our future?

830
00:59:35,197 --> 00:59:36,907
I'll become a burden to you,

831
00:59:38,117 --> 00:59:40,202
and you'll suffocate me.

832
00:59:41,912 --> 00:59:44,581
For three years, five years,

833
00:59:44,707 --> 00:59:46,917
or maybe even ten years,

834
00:59:47,042 --> 00:59:49,795
we'll keep trying for each other.

835
00:59:51,213 --> 00:59:52,298
But Namgung,

836
00:59:53,716 --> 00:59:55,217
in the end,

837
00:59:56,051 --> 00:59:57,469
we'll end up hating each other.

838
00:59:58,971 --> 01:00:00,097
No.

839
01:00:01,015 --> 01:00:03,475
Maybe we already do
and just don't know it.

840
01:00:06,729 --> 01:00:08,105
I don't want that.

841
01:00:10,357 --> 01:00:12,318
I don't want you to hate me.

842
01:00:13,485 --> 01:00:15,404
And I really don't want to hate you.

843
01:00:18,657 --> 01:00:20,659
So I don't want that future.

844
01:00:20,784 --> 01:00:23,537
I don't want to keep going
just to end up miserable.

845
01:00:25,789 --> 01:00:26,749
Why not?

846
01:00:28,834 --> 01:00:29,877
Are you scared?

847
01:00:32,421 --> 01:00:34,381
Does it scare you that much?

848
01:00:35,049 --> 01:00:37,134
More than breaking up with me?

849
01:00:39,178 --> 01:00:41,305
Yes, I'm scared.

850
01:00:42,723 --> 01:00:44,224
Aren't you scared?

851
01:00:45,059 --> 01:00:46,018
I am.

852
01:00:47,603 --> 01:00:48,937
I'm scared, too.

853
01:00:50,481 --> 01:00:51,523
But…

854
01:00:53,275 --> 01:00:55,110
I can't break up with you.

855
01:00:56,695 --> 01:00:58,781
You disappearing from my life

856
01:00:59,907 --> 01:01:01,700
scares me more, Mi-do.

857
01:01:05,037 --> 01:01:06,205
So I…

858
01:01:08,248 --> 01:01:09,833
Mi-do, I…

859
01:01:12,336 --> 01:01:14,088
I want to keep going with you.

860
01:01:17,841 --> 01:01:19,301
No matter how we end up,

861
01:01:19,426 --> 01:01:23,764
even if we're a total mess
at the end of it all,

862
01:01:26,266 --> 01:01:27,684
I still want to take this path.

863
01:01:35,609 --> 01:01:36,527
Let's get married.

864
01:01:40,906 --> 01:01:43,283
Let's get married, Mi-do.

865
01:01:46,537 --> 01:01:49,957
Marry me, Mi-do.

866
01:02:26,910 --> 01:02:28,245
THANK YOU TO CHO HAN-CHEUL, KIM DA-HUIN,
AND OH DONG-MIN

867
01:02:28,454 --> 01:02:29,496
FOR THEIR SPECIAL APPEARANCE

868
01:02:29,663 --> 01:02:31,123
WHEN THAT DAY COMES
MI-DO

869
01:02:31,248 --> 01:02:32,708
Namgung.

870
01:02:32,833 --> 01:02:34,960
I want that spark back with you.

871
01:02:35,085 --> 01:02:38,422
And I hope you feel it with me, too.

872
01:02:38,547 --> 01:02:39,631
His name is Namgung Ho.

873
01:02:39,756 --> 01:02:42,384
He'll be living with us starting today.

874
01:02:42,509 --> 01:02:44,678
Have you talked about that with Hoya?

875
01:02:45,262 --> 01:02:47,556
Hello. My name is Park Su-a.
I look forward to working with you.

876
01:02:47,681 --> 01:02:50,392
You're clingier than I thought, Ms. Park.

877
01:02:50,517 --> 01:02:52,895
Mr. Namgung. This is clear WH.

878
01:02:53,020 --> 01:02:54,146
I've looked into you too.

879
01:02:54,271 --> 01:02:57,107
Apparently, you do everything
Ju-hyeok tells you to.

880
01:02:57,232 --> 01:02:58,525
So I'm a dog?

881
01:02:59,526 --> 01:03:01,695
Hey. Look at you now.

882
01:03:02,821 --> 01:03:04,781
Subtitle translation by Cayle Kim
